  "sourceState": "Reports Wave A: the snapshot-marked report engine and all seven cartridges ported with the pinned financial-cluster inputs collapsed onto the Harborline-owned neutral IReportQuerySource port (migration reports WAVE-STATE ruling 1); 193/193 native cases green under their pinned names with per-class parity exact (the migration ledger’s 195 counted the abstract determinism harness as a concrete class — recorded accounting correction). Open-item queries are tenant+chart-scoped and ReportOpenItem carries both identities, restoring the pinned AP tenant-isolation semantics a draft pass had weakened. PrincipalId ported verbatim from packages/foundation/Crypto into hlp.contracts.identities (first consumer). blocks-reports-tax is deliberately absent (no pinned caller; deferred-capability register). The DI composition ported near-verbatim (already financial-cluster-free at the pin). Post-port hardening (ticket 081 wave 1, 2026-08-22): the suite grew 193->241 with the wave-1 findings closed — test-side bucket classification removed in favor of hand-pinned boundary literals, the shared fake classifies from the requested asOf and records markers/asOf observations, chart existence validated fail-closed in all seven cartridges (production change, TrialBalance pattern), MaxWarnings truncation and envelope exactness pinned, the seven kebab kind tokens pinned as persisted ticket-073 config keys, the unusable abstract determinism harness DELETED (record equality cannot compare list-bearing results) and replaced by per-cartridge determinism suites, and DI-resolved end-to-end dispatch tests added per cartridge. contentHashes re-recorded via record-dotnet-provenance.mjs; the extraction itself is unchanged (the upstream blob attestation this sentence once cited was retired by ticket 269, HLP-0007).",
